    "result_text": "The test passes.\n\nI implemented the home screen as a full-stack, additive change:\n\n**Backend** (new files, no edits to central infra):\n- `DashboardSummary.java` \u2014 record DTO with `clientsCount`, `projectsCount`, `outstandingTotal`.\n- `DashboardRepository.java` \u2014 counts clients/projects and sums UNPAID invoice amounts (`COALESCE(SUM(amount), 0)` so it's never null).\n- `DashboardGetLogic.java` + `rest/api/dashboard.GET.yml` \u2014 new `GET /api/dashboard` endpoint under `/api/` so it bypasses the SPA fallback.\n\n**Frontend** (new feature folder, auto-discovered by the router glob):\n- `features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx` \u2014 fetches the summary and renders the three anchors the spec expects: `dashboard-clients-count`, `dashboard-projects-count`, `dashboard-outstanding-total` (formatted to 2 decimals, e.g. `300.00`).\n- `features/dashboard/route.tsx` \u2014 registers `section: 'dashboard'` (giving `nav-dashboard`) with `order: 0` so it's the first nav item / landing page.\n\nNo schema migration was needed since the dashboard only reads existing tables, and the spec expects no audit records. `bin/e2e` passes (1/1).",
